{{also|tail-end|tailend}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|taylende}}; equivalent to {{af|en|tail|end}}.

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|tail-end|tailend}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The [[hindmost]] part of anything (a person, animal, or object), the [[butt]], [[buttocks]]; [[hindquarter]]s, [[rump]].
# {{lb|en|figurative}} The last part of a period of time, event, or situation; the concluding or final part.
#: ''At the '''tail end''' of summer. The '''tail end''' of a lecture. The '''tail end''' of a conversation.''
#* {{quote-web|date=2016-12-20|author=Katie Rife|title=Passengers strains the considerable charms of Chris Pratt and Jennifer Lawrence|site=The Onion AV Club|url=https://film.avclub.com/passengers-strains-the-considerable-charms-of-chris-pra-1798189990|passage=An equipment malfunction has woken him up 90 years early, and he’s now doomed to live out the rest of his life surrounded by '''sushi bars''' and infinity pools, but not a single human companion.(The other 5,000 passengers on board will wake up at the '''tail end''' of the ship’s 120-year voyage to Earth colony Homestead-II.)}}

